#######################################################################################################################
# as an additional safeguard in order to reveal potential time zone related bugs, comment this out one of the below
#   `TZ` environment variable to fake the default timezone.
# without it, developer in US can't discover the problem during regular working hour when the UTC date is still the 
#   same as the local date dispite the mismatch; but such flaky tests might start failing if run in other time frame.
#######################################################################################################################

## using GMT-1 is useful to reveal bug when production uses local while test uses UTC. (Note: this is in POSIX format, so it actually means 1 hours ahead of GMT instead of behind)
# TZ=GMT-1

## using GMT+23 is useful to reveal bug when production uses UTC while test uses local. (Note: this is in POSIX format, so it actually means 23 hours behind of GMT instead of ahead)
# TZ=GMT+23
